From 7bbe9f6cb34e73faf7ca8725f85ae0f38343a923 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lakitu12 <1219387824@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:07:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] um: accept 0x/0X in UML_HOST_TOP

The loader that synthesizes the kernel's initial stack prints addresses with
a %#x-style helper, so it hands the top over as UML_HOST_TOP=0x8000000000.
parse_host_top() took bare hex only: the 'x' failed the digit test and the
override became a silent no-op, sending the kernel back to the stack-derived
guess. With the app's environment one word larger that guess moved a page,
the stub placement moved with it, and bionic's own startup died in mmap
("failed to allocate bionic_tls") before the kernel printed anything -- the
exact failure this variable was added to prevent.

Accept the prefix when it is present instead of depending on which producer
is in use (bare hex keeps working; the loader still prints 0x).

Measured on marble (4 KB guest pages, app loader): with the prefix rejected,
kernel 4k-ht dies with bionic_tls before its first print; with the value
parsed, the same image boots to the guest's init (env, auxv, TMPDIR and
TASK_SIZE all correct).
---
 arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c b/arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c
index a84c450..cee30fc 100644
--- a/arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c
@@ -324,12 +324,22 @@ static int __init parse_host_cpu_line(char *line)
  * allocate bionic_tls") before printing anything. The value is authoritative
  * when present; the stack heuristic below stays as the fallback for a plain
  * `exec` of the kernel binary.
+ *
+ * The 0x/0X prefix is optional. It has to be: the app's loader prints the
+ * value with the very same %#x-style hex helper it logs addresses with, and
+ * a parser that took bare hex only turned the override into a silent no-op —
+ * the kernel went back to the stack heuristic and died in bionic startup
+ * again, which reads exactly like the bug this variable exists to prevent.
+ * Accept both forms rather than depend on which producer is in use.
  */
 static int __init parse_host_top(char *s, unsigned long *out)
 {
 	unsigned long v = 0;
 	int n = 0;
 
+	if (s[0] == '0' && (s[1] == 'x' || s[1] == 'X'))
+		s += 2;
+
 	while (*s) {
 		char c = *s++;
 		unsigned int d;
